  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 152 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nH5 ridge axis will push eastward but gradually de-amplify due to a \nfew short-wave perturbations coming out of the Pacific Northwest. But \nthrough the work week, this will push the thermal ridge far enough \neast to provide WAA, pushing temperatures back into the upper 70s, \nwith highs in lower 80s for points south of Interstate 70. Most the \nmid-level kinematic action is still progged to remain will north of \nthe area over the next 7 Days, and ensemble suites still keep \nprobabilities for measurable precipitation at 10 percent or less, \nand therefore will maintain a dry forecast. This should provide \nplenty of opportunity for the elevated river levels to continue to \nfall through this week. Breezy south to southwesterly winds will be \npossible on Tuesday as the surface anticyclone exits eastward \npushing a stronger pressure gradient through, along with boundary \nlayer mixing during the afternoon.",
